    family: 'A revealed alphabet, by Dee and Kelley’s account: recorded in manuscript in 1583, in John Dee’s record of his conversations with angels through the scryer Edward Kelley, and keyed to the Latin letters. It is not one of Agrippa’s alphabets. Wikipedia notes “many graphical similarities” with an alphabet ascribed to Enoch in Pantheus’s Voarchadumia (Venice, 1530), a book Dee owned, but no derivation is documented, and one direct comparison finds no letter that matches.',
